{
  "book": "RUT",
  "chapter": 3,
  "resources": {
    "costumbres": {
      "c-1bb6b5f0fca3876b": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-246",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "Mitpachath, veil, is called mantle in Isaiah 3:22 and some lexicographers assert that this is its meaning; that it does not signify what is commonly understood by a veil, but simply a large outer mantle or cloak, in one corner of which Ruth received the barley. Others, however, a…",
        "traduccion": {
          "resourceId": "freeman-246",
          "sourceHash": "1d7a0a0eb44c42c913099a015d5b048c0e42cab1a5740d97850bbdbd0fa8a071",
          "sourceLanguage": "en"
        }
      },
      "c-244e1cad5563498f": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-245",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "Some have supposed from the association of the goel with marriage, as in this history of Ruth, that it was his duty to marry the widow of a deceased kinsman: but according to Deuteronomy 25:5 this duty was only obligatory on a brother-in-law, which relation to Ruth was certainly…",
        "traduccion": {
          "resourceId": "freeman-245",
          "sourceHash": "bd24adae65fdf95ec6275930cd869611751fde3df5857001656c23ee44c8dfba",
          "sourceLanguage": "en"
        }
      },
      "c-994070bae154c45e": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-244",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "The threshing floor being uninclosed, (see note on Gen. 50:10 #101) and exposed to robbers, it was necessary for the proprietor or some trusty servant to keep up a watch. We therefore find Boaz taking his supper and sleeping at the end of the heap of corn. This is still done by t…",
        "traduccion": {
          "resourceId": "freeman-244",
          "sourceHash": "f37063e8c8ef706700344f2d37980cac84f0d2af08e06af95951a9a346b677e3",
          "sourceLanguage": "en"
        }
      },
      "c-fef8de12c7a063d4": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-243",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "The evening was selected not only because it was cooler than the day, but because of the increase of wind which enabled the husbandman to winnow more thoroughly. For the Oriental mode of winnowing see note on Amos 9:9 (#609) and on Matthew 3:12 (#634).",
        "traduccion": {
          "resourceId": "freeman-243",
          "sourceHash": "c1edfd8ac4df93df7b97f2604e44dc53a2aec2bb97f86fac670b56b0b7a27d0a",
          "sourceLanguage": "en"
        }
      }
    },
